<body>

<h1>⚛️ React.js Core Concepts & Machine Coding - Revision Notes</h1>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>Part 2 Master Revision Guide:</strong> React Elements, Components, JSX, State vs Props, Key prop, Controlled Forms, useEffect vs useLayoutEffect, The 4-Guard Search Architecture, Data Fetching, and Shimmer UI.
</div>

<h2>1. React Core Constructs</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>React Element:</strong> An immutable plain JavaScript object describing UI. Created via JSX or <span class="code">React.createElement()</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>React Component:</strong> A JavaScript function or class that returns React Elements and encapsulates logic.</li>
  <li><strong>React Node:</strong> Anything that can be rendered (elements, strings, numbers, arrays, null).</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. State vs Props & Immutability</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Property</th>
    <th>State</th>
    <th>Props</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Origin</strong></td>
    <td>Managed internally inside the component</td>
    <td>Passed down from parent component</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Mutability</strong></td>
    <td>Mutable via setter (<span class="code">useState</span>)</td>
    <td>Read-only (immutable for child)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>3. Lists & The Key Prop</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Purpose:</strong> Keys help React's <em>Reconciliation (Diffing Algorithm)</em> uniquely identify which list elements changed, were added, or were removed.</li>
  <li><strong>Why Array Index as Key is Bad:</strong> Reordering or deleting list items causes index mismatch, leading to unnecessary re-renders and wrong UI state bugs in inputs. Use unique IDs!</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Controlled Components & Search Filters</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Controlled Component:</strong> Input value is bound to React state (<span class="code">value={state}</span> + <span class="code">onChange</span>). Single source of truth.</li>
  <li><strong>The Input Freeze Trap:</strong> If <span class="code">value={text}</span> is provided without <span class="code">onChange</span>, typing is blocked and input freezes.</li>
  <li><strong>The 2-List Pattern:</strong> Keep two states in search filters: <span class="code">allRestaurants</span> (master copy, never mutated) and <span class="code">filteredRestaurants</span> (display copy).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. useEffect vs useLayoutEffect (PDF Q11)</h2>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>Feature</th>
    <th>useEffect</th>
    <th>useLayoutEffect</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Timing</strong></td>
    <td>Runs <strong>AFTER</strong> browser paint (Asynchronous)</td>
    <td>Runs <strong>BEFORE</strong> browser paint (Synchronous)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Blocking</strong></td>
    <td>Does not block paint (Smooth UX)</td>
    <td>Blocks paint until executed</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Best For</strong></td>
    <td>Data fetching, Timers, Event Listeners</td>
    <td>DOM measurements, Tooltip/Modal positioning (Prevents flickering)</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>6. Production Search Bar: The 4-Guard Architecture</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Debouncing:</strong> Waits for a pause (300ms) to throttle rapid typing bursts.</li>
  <li><strong>Min-Length Guard:</strong> Only query when <span class="code">searchText.length &gt;= 3</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>Search Caching:</strong> Cache results in an in-memory object so repeat searches execute in 0ms without network overhead.</li>
  <li><strong>AbortController (Race Condition Prevention):</strong> Cancel stale in-flight requests when a new search string is typed.</li>
</ol>

<h2>7. Asynchronous Data Fetching & Shimmer UI</h2>
<div class="callout">
  <strong>The 4-Step Mental Formula:</strong>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>3 States:</strong> <span class="code">data ([])</span>, <span class="code">isLoading (true)</span>, <span class="code">error (null)</span>.</li>
    <li><strong>useEffect:</strong> Trigger fetch inside <span class="code">useEffect(..., [])</span>.</li>
    <li><strong>Promise handling with .finally():</strong> Always set <span class="code">setIsLoading(false)</span> in <span class="code">.finally()</span>.</li>
    <li><strong>Render Order:</strong> Check error first, then loading, then actual UI.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

</body>
</html>
